CorpoWars3d is an original single-player tactical FPS adaptation of QSOLKCB/CorpoWars.
Its simulation, campaign, challenges, fictional setting and squad profiles derive
from CorpoWars at 815b609cd6c2eb5c789a78ebe3e91d0438807b79, Apache-2.0.
src/simulation.js is modified to hand a piloted agent's movement and trigger to
the FPS adapter, apply control before objective evaluation and reject direct
motion for stationary interactions. Campaign and challenge data retain the
original economy/save rules. CorpoWars3d adds finite city patrols, a relay
response and a manual Panic burst with a cooldown after the effect.

src/vendor/time.js is QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS's FixedClock, Apache-2.0, at
1f965f4e5b6669de0f954e3a39b11aa679e56720.
The new renderer adapts its retained-buffer capacity pattern and credits the
invariant-driven reuse concepts in QSOLKCB/OPT at
7556dd36acd53ed3ed538fd03b1db44e5c1ec869. No OPT donor source is copied.

src/controller.js adapts QUICKSCOPER standard gamepad sampling and radial sticks.
src/touch.js and src/devices.js adapt VANILLAJS neutral-input and pointer-ownership
patterns; no browser packages are introduced.

src/math.js, src/audio.js and src/music.js derive from QSOLKCB/QUICKSCOPER,
Apache-2.0, at 7c406e2545d82ee6bdc5fda5f198eb22fa183a84.
QUICKSCOPER's original raw WebGL pipeline and fixed-step FPS input boundaries
were consulted. The instanced city renderer, squad adapter and interface are new.

VANILLAJS and CorpoWars source notices credit rendering reuse to OPT's invariant/
signature concepts; no Wonderbuild or GPL donor source is copied. QUICKSCOPER
includes only original JavaScript, procedural geometry and synthesised audio.

Syndicate and FreeSynd are acknowledged solely as genre inspiration.
